nswer/id #uuid "3f07a31e-afd5-574c-b84a-4c775953dcd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099028} {:answer/id #uuid "7c282323-a32d-5969-83ed-d938a4ad4bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099029} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9ab6ce-37b7-526f-92ce-0279e52b7b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099030}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186099026} :answer-field/id #uuid "468f70d4-e1fe-51a6-a43a-7fc0681f374d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da3b0feb-e320-535c-8435-9a7c6b6e71cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-18650" :question/problem "![](images/3f/3f2d06871f14bead2e13d9fcb373560dcd74b30f74c3d8f9a6319762130ec162.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-3,3].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x)$, the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $4$ and $2$ respectively (from left to right). Find the maximum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,3]$ given that $f(-3)=-6.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the maximum value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,3]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-3,3),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=0.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-3,0,3.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =-6 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-3)+{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6-4 \\\\  & =-10 \\\\ f(3) & =f(-3)+{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6-4+2 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the largest value of $f$ from our candidates. \n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{max}}=\\max \\{-6,-10,-8\\}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{max}}=-6,$ and the value of $x$ that maximizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{max}}=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097bf9be-35d0-5117-aeeb-185f65a4e444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295316} {:answer/id #uuid "0c595f3e-4a64-5335-bfee-ef4f9c199d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295335} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9d8072-eeac-5190-ac53-423bbc5c0d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295602} {:answer/id #uuid "7c854fd3-91d0-5ade-bfec-4aa656855a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295948} {:answer/id #uuid "943f1ef0-98c7-561c-8c98-1ab90aa0f4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296059}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296059} :answer-field/id #uuid "94521d82-e55e-520c-aa39-65e9dae6d07e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bc1950d7-cc9c-5e9a-8f86-5dcc05de2e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-31329" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{\\log }_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={\\log }_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\log }_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {\\log }_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{\\log }_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27327c99-efb7-58e8-a74e-787cf861a36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295482} {:answer/id #uuid "87c24d2f-2c74-5040-90ac-f36195ad44b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295999} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd76f53-ed5e-50ea-9b0a-4825cbde5b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{log}_{3}^{2}⁡x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296097} {:answer/id #uuid "cee39ee1-4f54-5380-b841-9cb4997a9fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}){log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296353} {:answer/id #uuid "e80a0ef7-8043-5002-b2dc-df0cdf73346a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296500}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295999} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e8e1d5-6ca1-583b-a916-cb7fac5a8d3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d8e9ea16-ddaf-5f82-ac82-079325b04f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31401" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{\\log }_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={\\log }_{3}⁡({x}^{2}).$Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\log }_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {\\log }_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\int u\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{\\log }_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "934d0624-ee89-585f-9f2a-d9b229f6d4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.42 + 2.73\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099592} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d64a41-3d69-5acf-9172-fa5212236e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1.25 + 2.73\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099593} {:answer/id #uuid "cf085719-bf23-5682-a3a2-0a5f48bc1db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3.42 + 3.91\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099594} {:answer/id #uuid "4d09d2cd-648e-5ef9-8508-09eeea75ca3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1.25 + 0.91\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099595} {:answer/id #uuid "63aae9bf-7e43-5a52-bcdf-c2f1d11ac695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.42 + 0.91\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099596}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f76248ba-8061-5958-9a43-6adceb37c269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-fiel