eld/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154590}] :question/id #uuid "d664781c-c3c4-5a4a-b75b-80917efef798" :question/math-academy-id "q-225301" :question/problem "Let $a ∈ Z$. Prove that if $5∣a$ and $7∣a$, then $35∣a$.\n\nSince $5$ and $7$ are coprime, their {{field-1}} is given by\n$\\operatorname{lcm} (5, 7)$ {{field-2}} {{field-3}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f94be783-b301-53ba-a172-392e8da1d4db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291683}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291683} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c2b183c-4203-54db-8f85-5073cac6a682" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f408fcec-f9a2-541b-881a-ca675ec123e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291659} :answer-field/id #uuid "70f13110-b3f2-5149-b2c1-6fa4c9cab53f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e32140a-74e3-5010-9a04-c56681ce72f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291034} :answer-field/id #uuid "9307f284-f642-57d2-bdd2-2af6a8e5a778" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16949acc-a199-5034-b334-c8a926858464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290725} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb0a446c-185a-5e1d-9892-9ab8a1ed24e0" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acc7622d-e012-5706-814a-b7a1fcdc5d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291382}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291382} :answer-field/id #uuid "d089482d-8253-5abd-9483-4eb5d6cfb957" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b77a293-6401-5fc1-ae51-91e54401f0fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291153}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291153} :answer-field/id #uuid "e806e268-d324-5836-9b2c-598b0e75ad2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "629a23d1-2fb7-5c59-b550-e7888ca88598" :question/math-academy-id "q-252980" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right))=\\,\\,\n$$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}{J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & {J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\end{bmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)) & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right))\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right))\\,⊕\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the function of each Jordan block separately.\n\n- For ${J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right),$ we have $n=1$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $n=1,$ we don't need any derivatives. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For ${J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),$ we have $n=2$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $n=2,$ we need to compute the first derivative of $f$ only:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={\\sec }^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & {f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\ 0 & f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & {\\sec }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{1}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right))\\,⊕\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "837b084e-986c-5617-9260-46baeb2a4ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154725} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e54cb4-add1-57f4-a7c7-c98befd13ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154726} {:answer/id #uuid "04fdcb1f-1bc3-50ae-aedf-a5ac4159d293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154727} {:answer/id #uuid "09c3e908-922c-5709-89d4-258463ab4998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154728}] :answer-field/id #uuid "eb504893-8e7c-55fe-9925-a8a05d77e10d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8861d42f-fdfa-5386-9ad5-8f4af74480f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3^{32} \\cdot 3^{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154730} {:answer/id #uuid "9fb58e1c-1711-57f3-95a0-cc2ffee2e8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3^{16} \\cdot 3^{8} \\cdot 3^{4} \\cdot 3^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154731} {:answer/id #uuid "cdbde685-6baf-5805-9cd7-357de0512ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3^{32} \\cdot 3^{4} \\cdot 3^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154732} {:answer/id #uuid "f281d1a0-9b6f-5183-b71a-dfbdc3633fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3^{32} \\cdot 3^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154733}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5d7152e7-be73-5d08-8f35-a793e5071b49"