 [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9431c376-6b65-5c1c-abe5-8d53adefe289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517768} :answer-field/id #uuid "10722ede-227b-5ba8-9712-c73b71d70464" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "506f68f5-a23e-5a06-b8e8-1b3b16470943" :question/math-academy-id "q-254757" :question/problem "Suppose $a=[8,\\,4,\\,-3]^{T}$ and $b=[-4,\\,4,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Find the Chebyshev distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\n${d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Chebyshev distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty }\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{\\infty }=\\max (|{v}_{1}|,|{v}_{2}|,…,|{v}_{N}|).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{\\infty }(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & ={\\left\\|\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\|}_{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\max (|8-(-4)|,|4-4|,|-3-(-1)|) \\\\  & =\\max (12,0,2) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157711 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6122a7a-6b67-5f19-8a75-76dd0a6dbb78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551027}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551027} :answer-field/id #uuid "84463c14-3d13-5d9c-958d-8e0ba67632ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3f3dda19-f980-5165-8e4e-967243f6660c" :question/math-academy-id "q-254912" :question/problem "Suppose $a=[1,\\,-2]^{T}$ and $b=[-7,\\,8]^{T}.$ Find the Chebyshev distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\n${d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Chebyshev distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty }\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{\\infty }=\\max (|{v}_{1}|,|{v}_{2}|,…,|{v}_{N}|).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{\\infty }(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & ={\\left\\|\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\|}_{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\max (|1-(-7)|,|-2-8|) \\\\  & =\\max (8,10) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8eb9140-5069-521a-b617-e2778480f8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(12 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 9)\\bmod 37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154894} {:answer/id #uuid "d44fc1d9-1194-5f58-9988-7bbe036b71d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(7 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 15)\\bmod 37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154895} {:answer/id #uuid "23d713af-93c2-5162-b95d-5fdf2d098c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(33 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 9)\\bmod 37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154896} {:answer/id #uuid "2d310bd4-c55b-5849-9faa-87805d26593f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(12 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 3)\\bmod 37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154897} {:answer/id #uuid "7695bb32-8cfc-5200-82b3-60c63da3333f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(33 \\cdot 12 \\cdot 3)\\bmod 37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154898}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3b59cc08-f572-55bd-a2c9-254fc62bcd2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154893}] :question/id #uuid "4f1961bc-de8c-5868-a8aa-70f424928d88" :question/math-academy-id "q-258053" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $15^{26}\\bmod 37$?\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following table conta