ref 17592186488830}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488830} :answer-field/id #uuid "948cb113-9d46-5307-8103-2882839f19d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae53bd82-51d9-5e3a-a6c2-d93b776ac5e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-252986" :question/problem "What is the infimum of the set $A=\\{0,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9\\}?$\n\n$\\inf (A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a set $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the infimum of $A$ equals its minimum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\inf (A) & =\\min \\{0,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9\\}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162526 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f916cc-94f7-5a71-a178-e1e606a172ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-1\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489566} {:answer/id #uuid "266c7228-b4bb-5e08-96bf-a8a086712c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=0\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489601} {:answer/id #uuid "5295bbac-a212-512d-9607-9f1f6bb17448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489709} {:answer/id #uuid "cfcb399e-74da-5c9e-8dac-e3eed6a5f7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-1\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489976} {:answer/id #uuid "d5186c5a-5a30-5325-9bea-58622f595315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=0\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489987}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489709} :answer-field/id #uuid "598cb6fa-a32f-51ee-a272-ef449a513971" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "293c6e17-bbd1-5e99-90f1-bfcaef49f68c" :question/math-academy-id "q-253138" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi ),\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/bc/bcece2e5bdef3c9d939d953fbeb0c5163d9343004cd309f28db37bf9b5b089ef.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is an oscillating, non-convergent sequence. Moreover, $A$ is unbounded below. In other words, we can always find a sufficiently large $n$ so that ${a}_{n}$ is smaller than $x$ for any real number $x.$ Therefore, $A$ has no lower bounds and $\\inf (A)\\,=-\\infty .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff25cbe-96b0-5244-b7a8-2ae819809b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160497} {:answer/id #uuid "bf49f765-e10d-5efa-8f02-23884631cbb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160498} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a32217-222b-5694-b0e5-e9eef314a757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160499} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b61bea-0d92-5db0-8f02-d0fdb50f01f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160500}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186160499} :answer-field/id #uuid "b88ee89b-b237-5608-b215-04a9aa8e8677" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref