he {{field-1}} of $B$, and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $B$.\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-3}}, we have $\\inf (B)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-5}}, we have $\\sup (B)$ {{field-6}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc61529b-ed96-5458-8bb3-11fd45f62183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460377} {:answer/id #uuid "437dfb91-0f0f-5bb7-a172-620ce73392b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460377} :answer-field/id #uuid "11ef8e8f-82d4-56a1-96a7-0f3766f80afe" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to (0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9fa056e-9339-5f82-ad05-1ed3c4f6b7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460379} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a31e4c-e3f7-5f99-99c5-502a86e00ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460380}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460380} :answer-field/id #uuid "af15fbe2-a319-5181-a441-cbd348545c8b" :answer-field/key "$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "723033d0-1ec2-5946-b307-4de3fd9f066b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460381} {:answer/id #uuid "50df2fa7-6d3b-5ca7-8202-b268674641c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460382}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460382} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d1302fc-7564-51eb-b08f-34e05dc9d5d8" :answer-field/key "$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)={5}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93bb691b-3476-50ac-a75b-0f3bd8e04d2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-90713" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are **into** functions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- “$f:R\\to (0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$” is a *not* an into function. Given $y\\in (0,\\infty ),$ we can choose $x={\\log }_{2}⁡y\\in R.$ Then $f(x)=f({\\log }_{2}⁡y)={2}^{{\\log }_{2}⁡y}=y.$\n\n- “$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{4}$” is an into function. Let's take $2\\in Q.$ There is no number $x\\in Q$ such that $g(x)=2.$ The only numbers $x$ that satisfy $g(x)={x}^{4}=2$ are $x=\\pm \\sqrt[4]{2}\\notin Q.$\n\n- “$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)={5}^{x}$” is an into function. Let's take $-1\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in R$ such that $h(x)={5}^{x}=-1.$ In fact, ${5}^{x}>0$ for all $x\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{4}$”; “$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)={5}^{x}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162638 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7ccdba-167d-52d3-9f65-006af58a47df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448792} {:answer/id #uuid "45e79804-304f-56d7-91a8-584e5bc05ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448793}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448793} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fe36113-bf8a-58df-bd27-b2358ccf9634" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=9$ and $det(A)=18$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449436} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "695c1734-15fe-5bd0-a319-a113359ef2ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448794} {:answer/id #uuid "bb89c867-cc14-5d01-bdda-46476f5b4ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448795}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448795} :answer-field/id #uuid "83b596d7-227d-54aa-8cfb-eae069e9bd74" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf09e997-4a5d-5a14-a4c3-ad0a1321872f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448796} {:answer/id #uuid "09ac96d0-da48-5e6a-a5b5-c11c8827e02c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448797}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448796} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dba44f8-b993-5e8f-8c33-a9da0905d35e" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a27d2cf-0561-5715-9600-290d8804741e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94466" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=9$ and $\\det (A)=18$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=9$ and \n\n$$\n\\det (A)=\\begin{vmatrix}9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{vmatrix}=18.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” is true, while statement “$A$ is negative-definite” is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=9>0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =\\begin{vmatrix}9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{vmatrix}=18>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=9$ and $\\det (A)=18$”; “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162639 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8704f06e-0eca-5a70-9700-c5526052b2a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460407} {:answer/id #uuid "6518d566-4b59-5853-9f01-fa65f41a11a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460408}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460407} :answer-field/id #uuid "328cbc85-02de-5782-9f6f-1bfc8ec8fbb3" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-1$ and $det(A)>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b050a0c6-7aec-5f7e-8f14-b631435a1e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460409} {:answer/id #uuid "7dea8288-7e98-5761-9e3b-5108736ab6b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460410}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460410} :answer-field/id #uuid "147acc30-38f6-5dd4-b1fc-756ff6c1cd6a" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70cc8a99-fd5f-545d-944d-b10871efed96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460411} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4651ad-1ec2-5084-a1f5-126f6778fe6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460412}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460411} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6975a47-d056-596c-bc2f-5293e337fd67" :answer-field/key "$A$ is positive-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b242a4-d56a-55ce-8e1f-17ec28153e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668138} {:answer/id #uuid "08ca7ab6-0d10-52a3-9931-8c199021c084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668139}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186668138} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b9517d-8690-576c-a18e-f70b8b8be18f" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1a18cc33-e8b9-51a0-9ec6-b247bdd1e062" :question/math-academy-id "q-94467" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-1$ and $\\det (A)>0$” is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-1$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det (A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-4<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite” is true, while statement “$A$ is positive-definite” is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-1<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{vmatrix}=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-4<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162655 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2e3373e-36b0-5d84-9e12-7c37479aece9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.6824" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161223} {:answer/id #uuid "b03364e5-83ca-5894-afee-032021fcded9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.6616" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161224} {:answer/id #uuid "37ac3a4e-7d90-5d40-9e02-6baf810661ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.7817" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161225} {:answer/id #uuid "5029c6a1-697f-5d64-8192-e3cfb3d508d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.7165" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161226} {:answer/id #uuid "724076df-74b2-53c6-a073-49cc49606f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.7354" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161227}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b24b8e5a-d148-5ec4-90e5-47c2d38ff86a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "00460ff6-9869-572e-a081-8348a6b5f98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-95153" :question/problem "Given that t